  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 58. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. シロップ — 砂糖などを溶かした甘い液体。\n2. 白星 — 相撲などで勝ったことを表す印。\n3. 白身 — 卵の中で黄身を囲んでいる部分。\n4. 新型 — 新しい型や方式。\n5. 新居 — 新しく住む家。\n6. シンク — 台所などで水を使って物を洗う流し台。\n7. 真空 — 空気などの気体がほとんどない状態。\n8. 寝具 — 眠るときに使う布団や枕など。\n9. 新語 — 新しく使われるようになった言葉。\n10. 審査 — 基準に合わせて内容や出来具合などを調べること。\n11. 新作 — 新しく作った作品。\n12. 診察 — 医師が体の状態などを調べること。\n13. 寝室 — 眠るための部屋。\n14. 新車 — 新しく作られた車や使い始めたばかりの車。\n15. 親族 — 血縁や結婚などによってつながる人々。\n16. 寝台 — 寝るためのベッド。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
